Completed
Queue engine (upload/queue.ts): states queued, requesting, uploading, confirming, done, failed, rejected, cancelled.
Max 3 items at once and max 1 video at once (my chosen values, not validated on devices).
A signed URL is requested only after an item gets a slot, and the PUT starts immediately.
PUT failure retries with a new request and new mediaId. Confirm failure or timeout keeps the same mediaId, checks the server status first, and never re-uploads.
Local rejections use the spec copy. Server messages are shown as-is, never parsed.
Queued items can be cancelled; running PUTs can be aborted. Requesting and confirming cannot be cancelled.
Metadata:
Dependency-free EXIF reader for JPEG and HEIC/HEIF, reading small byte ranges only.
captured_at comes from EXIF DateTimeOriginal plus offset, else the browser time zone, else null. It is also null before 1990 or in the future; lastModified is never used.
Dimensions and duration are sanitised before sending.
Browser side:
XHR PUT of the original File with the same Content-Type and a 60 s stall watchdog.
Image and video dimensions are measured by browser decode, one image decode at a time.
Session end is detected with the browser getUser().
Refreshes are coalesced into one router.refresh() per 1.5 s window plus one on drain.
